# Upload filter for the Vercel project.
#
# The deployment is a single container image built from Dockerfile.vercel, so
# the build context must keep everything that Dockerfile copies: web/ (with its
# lockfile), src/, Cargo.toml, Cargo.lock, .cargo/ and deploy/. Docs, tests and
# local build output are dropped to keep the upload (and the docker context)
# small.

.git
.github
.githooks
docs
tests
scripts
book
book.toml
target
node_modules
web/node_modules
web/dist
render.yaml
.dockerignore

# The Render image keeps its own Dockerfile; the Vercel one must be uploaded.
/Dockerfile
!Dockerfile.vercel
